<section id="s-synthesis" data-code="synthesis">
<div class="section-no">06 — Synthesis</div>
<h2>DFlash++: A Proposed Recipe</h2>
<p>Bringing it together, a "DFlash++" system would combine all five LLaDA 2.x innovations with DFlash's parallel drafting architecture. Here is the proposed recipe, ordered by implementation complexity:</p>

<div class="step-list" id="recipe-steps">
  <div class="step-box active" id="recipe-step-0">
    <div class="step-num">1</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">WSD Initialization (LLaDA 2.0)</div>
      <div class="step-desc">Start from a small pre-trained AR model (e.g., 300–500M params) instead of random initialization. Convert via 3-phase WSD before DFlash fine-tuning. Expected gain: better draft quality in early training, potentially reducing required training data by 2–3×.</div>
      <div class="step-code">init = wsd_convert(ar_model_350M, phases=[warmup, stable, decay])</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="step-box" id="recipe-step-1">
    <div class="step-num">2</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">CAP Training (LLaDA 2.0)</div>
      <div class="step-desc">Add the confidence auxiliary loss to DFlash's existing CE + exponential-weighting loss. Sharpen predictions at correctly-predicted positions. Expected τ gain: +0.5–0.8 tokens (based on LLaDA 2.0's 1.9× TPF improvement extrapolated to acceptance rate).</div>
      <div class="step-code">loss = ce_loss + λ_cap * conf_loss(correct_positions)</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="step-box" id="recipe-step-2">
    <div class="step-num">3</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">T2T Training Mix (LLaDA 2.1)</div>
      <div class="step-desc">Add Token-to-Token editing stream alongside DFlash's mask-prediction training. At inference, run a second draft-model forward pass to edit uncertain positions. Expected τ gain: +0.8–1.2 tokens, especially on math/code tasks with strict token-exact requirements.</div>
      <div class="step-code">loss = ce_loss + α_t2t * t2t_edit_loss(perturbed_inputs)</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="step-box" id="recipe-step-3">
    <div class="step-num">4</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">EBPO Fine-tuning (LLaDA 2.1)</div>
      <div class="step-desc">After CE+CAP+T2T pre-training, run EBPO fine-tuning with the acceptance signal as reward. The verifier's accept/reject decisions are the most direct possible training signal for τ. Expected τ gain: +0.5–1.0 tokens over the CE baseline from direct objective alignment.</div>
      <div class="step-code">reward = sum(verifier_accept(draft, target)) / gamma</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="step-box" id="recipe-step-4">
    <div class="step-num">5</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">MBE: Multi-Block Lookahead (LLaDA 2.1)</div>
      <div class="step-desc">Allow the draft model to refine earlier blocks based on later-block context, catching global consistency errors. LLaDA 2.1 reports +2.0 pp at −11.7% TPF cost. For DFlash, MBE would only run when the draft model's confidence is low on earlier blocks, keeping the average overhead minimal.</div>
      <div class="step-code">if low_conf(draft[:k]): draft[:k] = mbe_refine(draft, context)</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
